cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this formalization, please cite it as below."
title: "Centrally-Excited-Random-Walk: a Lean 4 formalization of limit shapes of centrally excited random walks"
abstract: >-
  A machine-checked Lean 4 / mathlib formalization of the limit shape, fluctuation bounds and
  sharpness results for centrally excited random walk on Z^d, d >= 2, together with every lemma
  and proposition of the paper's Sections 2 to 9 and the limit shape for a walk whose drift is a
  subgradient of a norm. The production library contains no sorry and no custom axiom; the
  Mathlib-only comparator challenge contains one intentional statement-level sorry whose
  completed solution is checked separately.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bou-Rabee
    given-names: Ahmed
  - family-names: Peres
    given-names: Yuval
keywords:
  - Lean
  - mathlib
  - formal verification
  - excited random walk
  - limit shape
  - local time
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/nitromannitol/Centrally-Excited-Random-Walk"
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Kozma's centrally excited walk converges to a Euclidean ball"
    authors:
      - family-names: Bou-Rabee
        given-names: Ahmed
      - family-names: Peres
        given-names: Yuval
    notes: "The paper formalized by this repository; pinned at paper/limit-shapes.tex."
